KG42.register("rules-5bd363b4504efdaae7936e5c",{"id":"02-dlmp::v141-c-R005","paper":"02-dlmp","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"EV aggregators are assumed to participate as price takers without market power. Scope: Demand-side EV aggregators in the local DSO market under the proposed aggregator-based charging implementation. Condition: Each EV aggregator is assumed to control only a small portion of the EVs.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Demand-side EV aggregators in the local DSO market under the proposed aggregator-based charging implementation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E30"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"EV aggregators are assumed to participate as price takers without market power. Scope: Demand-side EV aggregators in the local DSO market under the proposed aggregator-based charging implementation. Condition: Each EV aggregator is assumed to control only a small portion of the EVs.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E27","v141-b-g01-E30"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p01-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":"203","section":"Abstract","anchor_text":"Abstract This paper presents an integrated distribution lo cational marginal pricing (DLMP) method d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In the proposed approach, the distribution system operator (DSO) determines distribution locational marginal prices (DLMPs) by solving the social welfare optimization of the electric distribution system which considers EV aggregators as price takers in the local DSO market and demand price elasticity."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":"206","section":"III. Aggregator-Based Optimal EV Charging Management","anchor_text":") charging management controlled by individual EV users, ag- 32) gregator-based charging management ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The EV charging management can take different forms: charging management controlled by individual EV users, aggregator-based charging management and proper mixture of the two mechanisms. In this paper, the aggregator-based EV charging management implementation is used. In the aggregator-based EV charging management concept, the EV aggregator is a profit-seeking entity who takes care of the EV fleet on behalf of the EV users, ensures that the energy needs are satisfied, and provides customized service and charging solution. The objective of EV aggregators is to meet the energy needs of EV users with the minimum charging cost. It is also assumed that each EV aggregator only controls a small portion of the EVs so that EV aggregators do not have market power and act as price takers in the DSO market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-16569f9a14-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"206","section":"III. Aggregator-Based Optimal EV Charging Management","anchor_text":"an- (38) is- EV ng (39) (40) 34) The constraints in (39) and (40) are to ensure that the EV charging","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"When the DLMPs, P_{DLMP,i,t}, are known to the EV aggregator, the optimization problem is a linear programming problem and the EV aggregator optimally decides x_{i,t}, the amount of energy to purchase in each hour, to minimize the charging cost subject to the charging power limit constraints and the driving requirement constraints."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This rule asserts a market-participation/admission assumption, not a decision. Its supporting passages (v141-b-g01-E01 'considers EV aggregators as price takers in the local DSO market'; v141-b-g01-E27 'each EV aggregator only controls a small portion of the EVs so that EV aggregators do not have market power and act as price takers in the DSO market'; v141-b-g01-E30 'the EV aggregator optimally decides x_{i,t}, the amount of energy to purchase in each hour') state the behavioral role rather than introduce a design-selection or operational variable within this rule's single-member scope participation.consumer. The symbol x_{i,t} that E30 names is the shared aggregator/clearing decision variable defined and owned by the coordination and clearing rules (v141-c-R004 and v141-c-R007), so per the shared-symbol rule it is not re-declared here without independent source scope for this rule.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed input or constant is defined by the price-taking/no-market-power participation assumption itself. The numeric constants that appear elsewhere in the mechanism (e.g., demand price elasticity -0.1 in v141-b-g02-E18; EV battery SOC bounds and charging limits in v141-b-g02-E19) parameterize the clearing/aggregator subproblems owned by other rules and are not given a scope for this participation rule, so no parameter object is transcribed here."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E27","quote":"It is also assumed that each EV aggregator only controls a small portion of the EVs so that EV aggregators do not have market power and act as price takers in the DSO market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E01","quote":"considers EV aggregators as price takers in the local DSO market"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E30","quote":"the EV aggregator optimally decides x_{i,t}, the amount of energy to purchase in each hour"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"4c0e6e208086f0a84267b0e846d7f981b295db51c3817c31abb6e16aae1ef836","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"Rule v141-c-R005 encodes a participation/admission assumption of the integrated DLMP mechanism (mechanism_id v141-a-M01, process_stage participation): EV aggregators participate in the local DSO market as price takers without market power, each controlling only a small portion of the EVs, under the aggregator-based charging implementation. The supplied (unreviewed) evidence states this only verbally: v141-b-g01-E01 says the social-welfare optimization 'considers EV aggregators as price takers in the local DSO market'; v141-b-g01-E27 says 'each EV aggregator only controls a small portion of the EVs so that EV aggregators do not have market power and act as price takers in the DSO market'; v141-b-g01-E30 says the aggregator, given the DLMPs, 'optimally decides x_{i,t}, the amount of energy to purchase in each hour, to minimize the charging cost'. None of these passages contains an equation expressing the price-taking / no-market-power condition, so no expression can be transcribed at source fidelity and the core constraint v141-c-R005-C001 is retained exactly as frozen (kind=procedural, role=core, expression=null, formalization_origin=not_formalized, template_id=null, members=['participation.consumer'], variable_refs=[], parameter_refs=[], evidence_ids=['v141-b-g01-E01','v141-b-g01-E27','v141-b-g01-E30']). The operational decision variable x_{i,t} (hourly energy purchased) and the aggregator linear program the E30 passage alludes to belong to the coordination/clearing rules (e.g., v141-c-R004 with equations (38)-(40), evidence v141-b-g01-E28 to v141-b-g01-E31; v141-c-R007), and are not re-declared or moved into this participation rule. Because the rule is a behavioral/admission assumption with no supported expression, applicability is non_mathematical with empty x and theta. All referenced B evidence carries source_status unverified under this experiment's policy; no independent source audit or correctness claim is made, and any missing or ambiguous content remains unresolved.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
